==English==

===Etymology===
Compare {{m|en|whale|t=something or someone excellent}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-have a whale of a time.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|have<has,,had> a whale of a time}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[enjoy]] oneself greatly.
#: ''We '''had a whale of a time''' at the party Saturday night.''

